  "goodToKnow": "Eingangs means at the beginning or outset, mainly in formal speech and writing: wie eingangs erwähnt (as mentioned at the beginning), a phrase used in presentations and essays to refer back. As a preposition with the genitive, it means at the start of: eingangs des Tals. Der Eingang is an entrance, and in business, receipt: nach Eingang der Zahlung (after receipt of payment)."
